I'm not doubting the damage potential of ranged attacks, I'm doubting
the person's ability to know which actions they should take.  For
example, if they are surrounded by 8 monsters, and they don't really
understand monster damage because they avoided melee range the whole
game, then they might not know which monsters they should attack, and
which monsters they should avoid, and which path they should take to
reach the summoner given the likely paths each of the monsters would
take when the player travels toward the summoner.  The result is that
even though they can do loads of ranged damage, they'll still get
buried in summoning storms.

Yes, ranged attacks can do lots of damage, but I think it stunts growth
to rely on it before you completely understand melee combat.  Players
are switching to the ranged bandwagon way too quickly, when they should
be learning how to melee before they switch to ranged.  And clearly,
they don't understand how melee combat works, because they've convinced
themselves that it is automatically too dangerous, which is completely
false for melee characters in most situations.  Seriously, melee
characters were designed for melee combat, and they do melee combat
quite well.  The game isn't so broken that the melee characters should
spend most of the game throwing projectiles.



